+---
+id: task-002-implement-json-patch-applypatch-rfc-6902
+type: task
+title: "Implement JSON Patch applyPatch (RFC 6902)"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Request
+
+Implement JSON Patch (RFC 6902). Export `applyPatch(document, patch)` from `src/index.ts`: it applies an
+array of operations (add, remove, replace, move, copy, test) to a JSON document and returns the result as
+a new value. It never mutates its input, and throws an error when the patch is invalid or an operation fails.
+
+# Acceptance
+
+- Patch must be an array of objects with a string `op` and a string `path` (valid JSON Pointer); unknown ops, and a missing `value` (add/replace/test) or `from` (move/copy), are invalid.
+- add: object member set/replaced; array insert at index (<= length) or `-` to append; "" replaces the document; parent must exist.
+- remove / replace: target must exist (remove of the whole document is rejected).
+- move / copy: `from` must exist; a move into its own child is an error; copy and values are deep-cloned (no aliasing).
+- test: deep JSON equality (object key order irrelevant); a mismatch throws.
+- Operations apply in order; any failure throws and the input is untouched. Keys such as `__proto__` are plain members.
+- Tests in `src/index.test.ts` cover the RFC 6902 Appendix A examples and error paths (`npm test`).
